---
/**
 * A stray bit: every so often a filled square glides across the page behind the
 * text, turning a few times at right angles on the way, with a fading trail.
 *
 * It is drawn on this canvas, which the script sizes to the screen as each trip
 * starts and pins to the page there, so a scroll carries the bit off with the
 * text around it. It never reaches past the page, so it never widens or
 * lengthens it, and it is hidden between trips. Its look and timing are
 * `data/bit.json`, tuned with the dev-only lab. See `scripts/bit.ts`.
 */
---

<canvas data-bit aria-hidden="true" hidden class="bit"></canvas>

<style>
  .bit {
    position: absolute;
    left: 0;
    /* Behind the page: the text and art paint over it, and the sticky nav, the
       one opaque surface, hides it. The black is the canvas, so it stays below. */
    z-index: var(--z-bit);
    pointer-events: none;
    /* One canvas pixel to a CSS pixel, scaled up without blurring on a dense
       screen: the bit is drawn in whole pixels. */
    image-rendering: pixelated;
  }
</style>

<script>
  import '@/scripts/bit'
</script>
